<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculate the conditional probability of two events, their complements and intersection</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A and B are two events such that p(A)={@prob_A@}, p(B)={@prob_B@} and p(A|B)={@prob_AgivenB@}</p>
<p>Find</p>
<p>a. p(B|A) = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>b.\( p(A^C∩B^C)\) = [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>c. \(p(A^C∩B)\) = [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked solution</b></p>
<p>a. Find \(p(B|A)\)</p>
<p>We have: \( p(B|A) =\frac{p(A\cap B)}{p(A)} \) (*) </p>
<p>We recall that \(p(A|B)=\frac{p(B \cap A)}{p(B)}\). So \(p(B \cap A)=p(A|B).p(B)\) (#)</p>
<p>When we substitute (#) in (*), we get \( p(B|A)=\frac{p(A|B).p(B)}{p(A)} \). Then</p>
<p>\(p(B|A)=\frac{({@prob_AgivenB@}).({@prob_B@})}{@prob_A@} \)</p>
<p>Therefore, \(p(B|A)={@ta1@}\)</p>
<hr>
<p>b. Find \( p(A^C \cap B^C)\)</p>
<p>We recall that \(p(A \cup B)+p((A \cup B)^C))=1\) but \((A \cup B)^C=A^C \cap B^C\).</p>
<p>Then \( p(A \cup B) + p(A^C \cap B^C)=1\)</p>
<p>Therefore, \( p(A^C \cap B^C)=1-p(A \cup B)\)
</p>
<p> \(p(A^C \cap B^C)=1-(p(A)+p(B)-p(A \cap B))\). Because \(p(A \cup B)=p(A)+p(B)-p(A \cap B)\).</p>
<p>Therefore, \(p(A^C \cap B^C)=1-( {@prob_A@}+{@prob_B@}-{@ta2_AnB@} )\)</p>
 <p>\(p(A^C \cap B^C)={@ta2@}\)</p>
<hr>
<p>c. Find \(p(A^C \cup B)\)</p>
<p>We get \(p(A^C \cup B)=p(B)-p(A \cap B)\).</p>
<p>Then, \(p(A^C \cup B)={@prob_B@}-{@ta2_AnB@}\)</p>
<p>Therefore, \(p(A^C \cup B)={@ta3@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
